# Scorecards — only change `.builder-main`

When implementing a Figma (or any design) for Scorecards, **only change `.builder-main`** in `src/prototypes/scorecards-v1-mvp/components/BuilderView.vue`.

That is the page body (breadcrumbs, title, actions, question list, detail). Everything around it is chrome and already correct.

## Leave these alone

- Global left nav (`LeftBar`)
- Admin sidebar (`.builder-admin-nav`)
- Call Review and Analytics views, unless the user explicitly asks

Figma files may show older or different sidebar, left menu, or shell artwork. **Ignore those differences.** The live chrome is the source of truth for every design going forward.

## Old Figma, modern visuals

Figma for `.builder-main` may also be old (wrong button color/size, darker input borders, pre-Dialtone styling). Keep the **layout and intent**. Restyle controls to current Dialtone using:

1. The cloned Scorecards prototype (`scorecards-v1-mvp` / original `scorecards`)
2. [dialtone.dialpad.com](https://dialtone.dialpad.com/)

Do **not** ship a version that looks meaningfully older or off-system. If the file would require that, **ask first**. The user may say the file is old — treat that as “take the spirit, update the visual language.”

## When to ask

- Chrome difference looks **major** (missing a whole nav, a different product shell)
- A `.builder-main` control would look older or unlike Dialtone / the existing prototype

Default: ignore outdated chrome; modernize outdated builder-main styling.
